      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): handle stdin stream errors in docker sandbox execution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`execDockerRaw` writes input to `child.stdin` but does not listen for stdin error events. If the stdin stream fails (e.g., broken pipe), the error is not handled and can become an unhandled exception.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd an explicit `stdin.on(\"error\", ...)` listener that records the error so the existing close-time error handling rejects the command result, matching the stdout/stderr stream error behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDocker sandbox execution is more resilient to transient stdin stream failures.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added regression test in `src/agents/sandbox/docker.stdin-stream-errors.test.ts`.\n- Added real behavior proof at `scripts/proof/docker-stdin-stream-errors.mts`.\n- Local run:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sandbox/docker.stdin-stream-errors.test.ts` passed\n  - `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/agents/sandbox/docker.ts src/agents/sandbox/docker.stdin-stream-errors.test.ts scripts/proof/docker-stdin-stream-errors.mts` passed\n  - `node --import tsx scripts/proof/docker-stdin-stream-errors.mts`:\n\n```\n=== Proof: docker stdin stream error catch ===\n\nRejected as expected: stdin write failed\n\nPASS: execDockerRaw caught the stdin error and killed the child.\n```",
        "branch": "fix/docker-stdin-stream-errors",
        "head_sha": "d2dcc640710d0b08411e2c85188da7b8b1907ea5",
